    "probe_text": "Here's the complete ordered trace of `POST /api/owners`, reading the pipeline in `owners.POST.yml` step by step. Validations throw (\u2192 HTTP error); side-effects mutate the request/owner or the datastore.\n\n## 0. Before the pipeline \u2014 authorization\n- **`composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`** \u2014 the whole endpoint is guarded; a caller lacking that role is rejected (403) before any step runs.\n\n## 1. `validate` \u2014 `ValidateOwnerFields`\nRuns in this internal order:\n1. **Side-effect \u2014 normalize address** (`OwnerAddress.normalize`): trim, collapse internal whitespace, upper-case, expand street abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`); written back onto the request. (Done first so the blank-check sees the normalized value.)\n2. **Validation \u2014 required fields**: `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-null and non-blank. All offenders are collected and reported together \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400).\n3. **Side-effect + validation \u2014 telephone to E.164** (`OwnerTelephone.toE164`): strip spaces/dashes/brackets, assume `+61` if no `+`, drop a leading national `0`; must be 8\u201315 digits, and for known country codes an exact national length (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400). The normalized value is written back onto the request.\n4. **Side-effect + validation \u2014 email** (`OwnerEmail.normalize`): only if present. Trim, must match the address regex, then lower-case; domain must not be on the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Invalid/disposable \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (400). Lower-cased value written back. Absent email left untouched.\n5. **Validation \u2014 postcode** (`OwnerPostcode.validate`): only if present. Must be exactly 4 digits; if the city maps to a known region, must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Invalid \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400). Postcode is **not** modified.\n6. **Side-effect \u2014 republish** the validated request as a variable for later steps.\n\n## 2. `registrationDate` \u2014 `ResolveRegistrationDate`\n- **Validation \u2014 not in the future**: a supplied `registrationDate` after the server's current date \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n- **Side-effect \u2014 resolve + roll to business day**: effective date = supplied, else today; a Saturday/Sunday is rolled forward to Monday (`BusinessDay.adjust`); published as a `LocalDate` variable.\n\n*(Steps 3\u201314 below are all governed by `transaction`, so they share one transaction that commits once at the end.)*\n\n## 3. `cityCapacity` \u2014 `CheckCityCapacity`\n- **Validation**: counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); `>= 50` \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n## 4. `dailyLimit` \u2014 `CheckDailyOwnerLimit`\n- **Validation**: counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the adjusted date; `>= DAILY_LIMIT` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429).\n\n## 5. `build` \u2014 `BuildOwner`\n- **Side-effect**: map the request DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity (`OwnerMapper`), set its `registrationDate` to the adjusted date, publish the `Owner` variable.\n\n## 6. `household-assign` \u2014 `AssignHousehold`\n- **Side-effect**: set `householdId` = first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode` (`OwnerIdentities.householdId`). Assigned to every owner.\n\n## 7. `identity` \u2014 `CheckUniqueIdentity`\n- **Validation**: if `sharesHousehold=true`, bypass. Otherwise, if the new owner's `householdId` matches any existing owner's \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n\n## 8. `possibleDuplicate` \u2014 `CheckPossibleDuplicate`\n- **Side-effect** (soft, non-blocking): if `sharesHousehold=true`, set `possibleDuplicate=false`, `possibleDuplicateOf=null`. Otherwise scan for an existing owner with the same last name + postcode but a **different** telephone; if found, set `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` = earliest matching owner id.\n\n## 9. `customerCode` \u2014 `AssignCustomerCode`\n- **Side-effect**: set `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` \u2014 region from postcode (falling back to city), HASH8 = first 8 upper-case hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`.\n\n## 10. `membershipNumber` \u2014 `AssignMembershipNumber`\n- **Side-effect**: set `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where YY is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year.\n\n## 11. `namesakes` \u2014 `CountNamesakes`\n- **Side-effect**: set `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing the same first + last name (case-insensitive; excludes the not-yet-saved new owner).\n\n## 12. `bulkSignup` \u2014 `FlagBulkSignup`\n- **Side-effect**: set `bulkSignupWarning` = `true` when more than 80 existing owners already share the adjusted `registrationDate`, else `false`.\n\n## 13. `save` \u2014 `SaveOwner`\n- **Side-effect**: persist the owner (`ownerRepository.save`).\n\n## 14. `respond` \u2014 `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n- **Side-effect**: `HouseholdMembers.stamp` sets `householdMemberCount` by counting stored owners with the same `householdId` (now includes the just-saved owner).\n- **Side-effect**: emit an `AUDIT` log line (id, customerCode, registrationDate, and computed membership level via `MembershipLevels.levelFor`).\n- **Side-effect**: map to `OwnerDto` and send **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the DTO body. The transaction commits here.\n\n---\n\n**Two things worth flagging:**\n- The order is deliberate \u2014 inside `validate`, address normalization precedes the blank-check (so an all-whitespace address is caught), and `registrationDate`'s future-check happens before the business-day roll. Across steps, all rejections (400/409/429) occur before `save`, so nothing invalid is persisted.\n- `membershipLevel`/`membershipPoints` are **derived on read** (`MembershipLevels`, used in the audit log and DTO mapping), not stored fields set by a pipeline step. A brand-new owner never earns the tenure points (zero tenure today)."
